For raw video, the calculation extends across time:ext{Video Size (bits)} = \text{Width} \times \text{Height} \times \text{Channels} \times \text{Bit Depth} \times \text{Frame Rate} \times \text{Duration}

If one minute of video is recorded at 1920 by 1080 resolution, in RGB color, with 8 bits per channel and 30 frames per second, then the raw data size is:1920 \times 1080 \times 3 \times 8 \times 30 \times 60 = 89{,}579{,}520{,}000 \text{ bits}

